      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 American College of Foot and Ankle Surgeons. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Cementoplasty is a well-established intervention for symptomatic control of localized skeletal metastases; however, its use has never been reported for metastases in the foot. We report on a patient with symptomatic skeletal metastases throughout the foot in which cementoplasty, in conjunction with internal fixation, was used to alleviate pain and enable comfortable ambulation."
      },
